%N A398437 Least value of x+y for 0<x<y such that (x^p+y^p)/(x+y) is prime, where p=prime(n), n>1; -1, if no such pair exists.
%H A398437 Jean-Marc Rebert, <a href="/A398437/a398437_1.txt">Data file showing a(n), x, and y values through a(100)</a>
%e A398437 a(2) = 1 + 2 = 3, because prime(2) = 3 and (1^3 + 2^3)/(1 + 2) = 3 is prime.
%e A398437 a(10) = 1 + 7 = 8, because prime(10) = 29 and (1^29 + 7^29)/(1 + 7) = 402488219476647465854701 is prime.
%e A398437 And no lesser x + y have this property.
